        <%# Rendered at build time from the same data the test runs on, so the copy and
        the test can never drift apart. This is also the only place a crawler that does
        not execute JavaScript can see what the Host category actually checks.
        Each require() must stay on its own single line: template-ejs-loader rewrites
        the path only when require() and the EJS tags share a line. %>
        <% const adblock_data = require('./data/adblock_data.json') %>
        <% const CATEGORY_LABELS = require('./data/category_labels.json') %>
        <%
        const categories = Object.keys(adblock_data).map((key) => {
            const brands = Object.keys(adblock_data[key])
            const hosts = brands.reduce((n, b) => n + adblock_data[key][b].length, 0)
            return { key: key, label: CATEGORY_LABELS[key] || key, brands: brands, hosts: hosts }
        })
        const totalHosts = categories.reduce((n, c) => n + c.hosts, 0)
        const totalBrands = categories.reduce((n, c) => n + c.brands.length, 0)
        %>
        <section class="seo_content better_r">
            <h2>What this ad blocker test checks</h2>
            <p>Three independent checks, scored together. No real ads or trackers are ever loaded.</p>
            <div class="checks_grid row keep-width">
                <div>
                    <div class="card _h-100">
                        <h3>Cosmetic filters</h3>
                        <p>Two ad-shaped elements, one static and one added after load. The test measures whether your blocker removes or hides them.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="card _h-100">
                        <h3>Ad script loading</h3>
                        <p>Two decoy scripts named <code>ads.js</code> and <code>pagead.js</code>. The test measures whether they were stopped from running.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="card _h-100">
                        <h3>Host and DNS blocking</h3>
                        <p><%= totalHosts %> hostnames across <%= totalBrands %> ad, analytics, tracking and telemetry services. This is the only category a DNS filter can score on.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <h3 class="hosts_head">The <%= totalHosts %> hosts, by category</h3>
            <ul class="hosts_list">
                <% categories.forEach(function (c) { %>
                <li>
                    <b><%= c.label %></b>
                    <span class="hosts_count"><%= c.hosts %> hosts</span>
                    <span class="hosts_brands"><%= c.brands.join(', ') %></span>
                </li>
                <% }) %>
            </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="seo_content better_r">
            <h2>Testing a DNS filter: Pi-hole, AdGuard Home, NextDNS, AdGuard DNS or Control D</h2>
            <p>A DNS filter blocks domains, so it can only pass the Host category. Here is the score to expect and how to read it.</p>
            <div class="dns_grid row keep-width">
                <div>
                    <div class="card _h-100">
                        <h3>What a good Pi-hole score looks like</h3>
                        <p>A DNS filter on its own answers <%= totalHosts %> of the <%= totalHosts + 4 %> checks, so <b>roughly 40&ndash;60% is the correct result</b>, not a failure. The four cosmetic and script checks need a browser extension, which no DNS resolver can do. If you want to know whether your Pi-hole is working, look at the Host category, not the total.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="card _h-100">
                        <h3>Turn the block page off first</h3>
                        <p>Pi-hole, AdGuard Home and NextDNS can answer a blocked domain with their own block page instead of dropping the request. To this test that looks like a <em>successful</em> connection, so your score drops even though the domain was blocked. Set the blocking mode to NXDOMAIN or NULL and re-run.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="card _h-100">
                        <h3>Getting to a full score</h3>
                        <p>Pair the DNS filter with a browser extension such as uBlock Origin or the AdGuard extension. The DNS layer covers the hosts, the extension covers the cosmetic filters and the ad scripts. That combination is what scores green here.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p class="dns_note">Written Pi-hole, pi-hole or pihole &mdash; all the same thing, and the same advice applies to AdGuard Home, AdGuard DNS, Control D, Quad9 and any other resolver-level blocker. The test cannot see per-client rules, regex filters or allowlists &mdash; only whether the <%= totalHosts %> hostnames above resolved.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="seo_content better_r">
            <h2>Ad blocker test FAQ</h2>
            <p>Answers about how the test works, what your score means, and how to improve it.</p>
            <div class="faq_list">
                <details>
                    <summary>How does the ad blocker test work?</summary>
                    <div>One click runs three independent checks and scores how much of your setup blocks ads and trackers. No real ads or trackers are ever loaded during the test.</div>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>My ad blocker is configured correctly but the test does not work. Why?</summary>
                    <div>Your configuration may not be compatible with the type of checks this tool performs. This does not mean your ad blocker is not providing protection. JavaScript limitations or missing features may prevent the test from accurately determining blocked connections. You will still receive an estimate of the percentage of connections blocked.
                        <div class="_py-1"><button data-a11y-dialog-show="dlg_compatibility">
                                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon icon-tabler icon-tabler-info-square" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                                    <path stroke="none" d="M0 0h24v24H0z" fill="none"></path>
                                    <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12.01" y2="8"></line>
                                    <rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="2"></rect>
                                    <polyline points="11 12 12 12 12 16 13 16"></polyline>
                                </svg> Check compatibility</button></div>
                    </div>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>How can I get 100% on the ad blocker test?</summary>
                    <div>A green score indicates satisfactory protection and there is no need to aim for 100%. However, if you want a perfect score, you can use the Turtlecute Host List which covers most of the host tests on the site (excluding cosmetic filters and script loading).
                        <div class="grid keep-width _mt-1">
                            <div>
                                <button class="btn-blue" id="hostListTxt">
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon icon-tabler icon-tabler-copy" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                                        <path stroke="none" d="M0 0h24v24H0z" fill="none"></path>
                                        <rect x="8" y="8" width="12" height="12" rx="2"></rect>
                                        <path d="M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2"></path>
                                    </svg>
                                    Turtlecute Host List (TXT)</button>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <button class="btn-blue" id="hostListAdblock">
                                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon icon-tabler icon-tabler-copy" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                                        <path stroke="none" d="M0 0h24v24H0z" fill="none"></path>
                                        <rect x="8" y="8" width="12" height="12" rx="2"></rect>
                                        <path d="M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2"></path>
                                    </svg>
                                    Turtlecute Host List (ADBLOCK)</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </details>
                <%- include('partials/adblock/faq.ejs') %>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>
    <%- include('partials/adblock/results.ejs') %>
    <% const adblock_compatibility = require('./data/adblock_compatibility.json') %>
    <div class="dialog" id="dlg_compatibility" data-a11y-dialog="dlg_compatibility" aria-labelledby="dlg_compatibility-title" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="dialog-overlay" data-a11y-dialog-hide></div>
        <div class="dialog-content">
            <header>
                <h3 id="dlg_compatibility-title">Tested setups</h3>
                <button data-a11y-dialog-hide aria-label="Close compatibility table dialog"><svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
                        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12">
                        </path>
                    </svg></button>
            </header>
            <%
            const PLATFORM = { macos: 'macOS', ios: 'iOS', android: 'Android', windows: 'Windows', windows11: 'Windows 11', 'linux(mint)': 'Linux' }
            const BROWSER = { brave: 'Brave', safari: 'Safari', chrome: 'Chrome', firefox: 'Firefox', edge: 'Edge', kiwibrowser: 'Kiwi' }
            function prettyLabel(token) {
                const i = token.lastIndexOf('-')
                if (i > 0) {
                    const b = token.slice(0, i)
                    const p = token.slice(i + 1)
                    if (BROWSER[b] && PLATFORM[p]) return BROWSER[b] + ' on ' + PLATFORM[p]
                }
                if (PLATFORM[token]) return PLATFORM[token]
                const words = token.replace(/-/g, ' ')
                return words.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + words.slice(1)
            }
            const RANK = { ok: 0, mixed: 1, bad: 2 }
            const STATE_LABEL = { ok: 'Test works', mixed: 'Some limits', bad: 'Cannot test' }
            const ICON = { dns: `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path stroke="none" d="M0 0h24v24H0z"/><path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 18 0 9 9 0 1 0-18 0M3.6 9h16.8M3.6 15h16.8"/><path d="M11.5 3a17 17 0 0 0 0 18M12.5 3a17 17 0 0 1 0 18"/></svg>` }
            const kinds = [
                { state: 'mixed', icon: ICON.dns, name: 'Pi-hole, AdGuard Home and other DNS filters', type: 'Pi-hole, AdGuard Home, AdGuard DNS, NextDNS, Control D, Quad9', desc: 'Not tested one by one. A DNS filter can only answer the Host category, so roughly 40–60% is the correct result for one on its own, not a failure. If the filter replies with its own block page instead of dropping the request, that looks like a successful connection here and the score drops further — set the blocking mode to NXDOMAIN or NULL. Add a browser extension to cover the cosmetic and script checks.' }
            ]
            const products = Object.keys(adblock_compatibility)
                .filter((k) => k !== 'default' && adblock_compatibility[k].hidden !== true)
                .map((k) => {
                    const v = adblock_compatibility[k]
                    const ok = v['no-issues'] || []
                    const mixed = v['m-issues'] || []
                    const bad = v['issues'] || []
                    const state = ok.length === 0 ? 'bad' : mixed.length || bad.length ? 'mixed' : 'ok'
                    const type = v.name.toLowerCase().includes(v.type.toLowerCase()) ? '' : v.type
                    return { state: state, icon: v.icon, name: v.name, type: type, ok: ok, mixed: mixed, note: v.note }
                })
            const rows = kinds.concat(products).sort((a, b) => RANK[a.state] - RANK[b.state])
            %>
            <section>
                <div class="compat_wrap">
                    <p class="compat_lead">Green means the test can measure that setup. Yellow and red only mean the test cannot see everything. Your blocker can still protect you well.</p>
                    <ul class="compat_list">
                        <% rows.forEach(function (r) { %>
                        <li class="compat_item">
                            <span class="compat_ico" aria-hidden="true"><%- r.icon %></span>
                            <span class="compat_head">
                                <b class="compat_name"><%= r.name %></b>
                                <% if (r.type) { %><span class="compat_type"><%= r.type %></span><% } %>
                            </span>
                            <span class="compat_state _<%= r.state %>"><%= STATE_LABEL[r.state] %></span>
                            <span class="compat_body">
                                <% if (r.desc) { %>
                                <span class="compat_on"><%= r.desc %></span>
                                <% } %>
                                <% if (r.ok && r.ok.length) { %>
                                <span class="compat_on"><span>Works on</span> <%= r.ok.map(prettyLabel).join(', ') %></span>
                                <% } %>
                                <% if (r.mixed && r.mixed.length) { %>
                                <span class="compat_on"><span>Unreliable on</span> <%= r.mixed.map(prettyLabel).join(', ') %></span>
                                <% } %>
                                <% if (r.state !== 'ok' && r.note && r.note.trim()) { %>
                                <span class="compat_note"><%- r.note %></span>
                                <% } %>
                            </span>
                        </li>
                        <% }) %>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="compat_lead">Two blockers at the same time can also give a wrong score.</p>
                </div>
            </section>
            <footer>
                <button data-a11y-dialog-hide aria-label="Close dialog">
                    Close
                </button>
            </footer>
        </div>
    </div>
    <%- include('partials/support_me.ejs') %>
    <%- include('partials/adblock/changelog.ejs') %>
    <%- include('partials/adblock/logs.ejs') %>
    <%- include('partials/footer.ejs') %>
    <%- include('partials/gotop.ejs') %>

</body>

</html>
